# Keep every text file LF in the repository AND in working copies.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which would check files out as CRLF on Windows. That is
# harmless for the JavaScript, but fatal for install.sh: a CRLF shell script fails on Linux with
# "bash\r: No such file or directory" or a cryptic `set -euo pipefail\r: command not found`.
# install.sh is the one path in this project that has never been executed, so it gets no second
# chance to be diagnosed — it is forced to LF here rather than left to a local git setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The design sheets are binary; never let git rewrite their line endings.
*.png binary
